Description: quit when the window is closed
 Only the Escape key stops the demo. Closing the window with the window
 manager destroys it, but gtk_main() keeps running and the process stays in
 the background. Call gtk_main_quit() on the destroy signal (the 4k build
 is left untouched, as it is not packaged).
Author: Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>
Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-14
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -155,6 +155,9 @@
   g_signal_connect (area, "realize", G_CALLBACK (realize), NULL);
   g_signal_connect (area, "render", G_CALLBACK (render), NULL);
   g_signal_connect (window, "key-press-event", G_CALLBACK(key_press), area);
+#ifdef DEBUG
+  g_signal_connect (window, "destroy", G_CALLBACK(gtk_main_quit), NULL);
+#endif
 
   gtk_widget_show_all(window);
 
